      "body": "## Motivation\r\n\r\nMamba2 hybrid models (Granite 4.0-H, Falcon-H1, Nemotron-H) do not start on ROCm. `mamba.py` binds `causal_conv1d_fn`, `causal_conv1d_update` and their Triton variants only in its CUDA, NPU and XPU branches, so on ROCm none of them is defined. The server fails while capturing the decode CUDA graphs:\r\n\r\n```\r\nNameError: name 'causal_conv1d_update_triton' is not defined\r\n```\r\n\r\n(`causal_conv1d_update` for Falcon-H1). `mamba1.py` imports those names from `mamba.py`, so it cannot be imported on ROCm either (\"Ignore import error when loading sglang.srt.models.mamba\").\r\n\r\n`causal_conv1d.py` already handles ROCm: the compiled kernel is CUDA-only, and it falls back to the Triton kernels there.\r\n\r\n## Modifications\r\n\r\n- `mamba.py`: take the CUDA import branch on ROCm too (`is_cuda_alike()`).\r\n- No change on CUDA, NPU, XPU or CPU.\r\n\r\n## Accuracy Tests\r\n\r\nMI350X, `rocm/sgl-dev:v0.5.21-rocm724-mi35x-20261012` with this change applied, `--attention-backend triton`.\r\n\r\n| Model | before | after |\r\n| --- | --- | --- |\r\n| `tiiuae/Falcon-H1-7B-Instruct` | NameError at startup | serves; GSM8K (all 1,319 questions, temperature 0, `sgl-eval` 0.1.2): 85.82% |\r\n| `ibm-granite/granite-4.0-h-tiny` | NameError at startup | starts and serves with `--enable-deterministic-inference`; in normal mode it then stops at a separate MoE `torch.compile` error (`moe_sum_reduce_torch_compile`), not addressed here |\r\n| `nvidia/NVIDIA-Nemotron-Nano-9B-v2` | NameError at startup | needs ReLU2 on ROCm as well (#44198) |\r\n\r\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\r\n\r\nNo performance change on other platforms; on ROCm these models did not run before.\r\n\r\n## Checklist\r\n\r\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\r\n- [ ] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\r\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\r\n- [x] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\r\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\r\n\r\n## Review and Merge Process\r\n\r\n1. Ping Merge Oncalls to start the process. See the [PR Merge Process](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/MAINTAINER.md#pull-request-merge-process).\r\n2. Get approvals from [CODEOWNERS](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/CODEOWNERS) and other reviewers.\r\n3. Trigger CI tests with [comments](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#how-to-trigger-ci-tests) or contact authorized users to do so.\r\n   - Common commands include `/tag-and-rerun-ci`, `/tag-run-ci-label`, `/rerun-failed-ci`\r\n4. After green CI and required approvals, ask Merge Oncalls or people with Write permission to merge the PR.",
